==============================================================================================================================
0.  AN INDEPENDENT IMPLEMENTATION OF g06's DWARF-SPHEROIDAL PREDICTION
==============================================================================================================================
  Re-coded from the physics, not copied from g06: a different radial grid (linear-in-u = ln r, Simpson),
  a different integration of the Jeans tail, and closed-form cross-checks in both limits.
  independently recomputed baryonic LSS field at the Local Group: g_B = 6.0245e-15 m/s^2 = 0.000064 a_0   (g06 printed 6.024e-15 = 0.00006 a_0)
  [PASS] V0 the external LSS baryonic field is reproduced, so any disagreement below is about the dwarf-spheroidal prescription and not about the field this file inherited   (this file 6.0245e-15 vs g06 6.024e-15, ratio 1.0001; it is 0.42% of the Milky Way's field at 76 kpc, i.e. irrelevant to the dwarfs)

==============================================================================================================================
1.  ANALYTIC CROSS-CHECKS OF THE INDEPENDENT SOLVER, IN BOTH LIMITS THAT MATTER HERE
==============================================================================================================================
  [PASS] A1 the independent Jeans quadrature reproduces the isolated deep-MOND virial sigma^4 = (4/81) G M a_0 for Draco's baryons.  This is g06's own J2, re-derived on a different grid and a different quadrature rule   (independent solver 3.690 km/s vs Milgrom 1994 analytic 3.652 km/s, ratio 1.0103  (g06 reported 3.690 vs 3.652, ratio 1.0104))
  [PASS] A2 in the external-field-dominated limit the field is quasi-Newtonian with a CONSTANT boost nu(e_N)(1+L(e_N)/3), so the Plummer virial sigma^2 = nu_eff pi G M/(32 a) must be recovered.  Draco is the object that drives g06's median, and this is the closed form that tells us why   (solver 1.940 km/s vs closed form 1.978 km/s (nu_eff = 7.212 at e_N = 0.01547); the residual difference is the internal field inside nu's argument at small r, which the closed form drops)

==============================================================================================================================
2.  THE EIGHT NUMBERS, RE-DERIVED.  DOES THE ARITHMETIC HOLD?
==============================================================================================================================
    dwarf           x_int(rh)       e_N  e_N/x_int  sig_pred  dex(this)  dex(g06)    diff
    Draco             0.00249   0.01554       6.25      1.94     +1.343    +1.343  +0.000
    Sculptor          0.01203   0.01215       1.01      4.71     +0.581    +0.581  +0.000
